Performance: Writing into a caller's `IBufferWriter<byte>`, growing pooled buffers, copying multi-segment sequences and reading new `BitArray`s use Nino's block copy instead of .NET's `Memmove`: on GitHub's runners (AMD EPYC 7763 and 9V74, Intel Xeon 8573C, Neoverse-N2) writing an int array into an external buffer is 1.07-1.41x faster and a `Memory<byte>` payload 1.09-1.45x faster; other cases are on par.
